title: Overview - Vocabularies & Markers (v1.0)

''Narrative intro to the v1.0 concept — read this first.'' For the full field reference see [[Overview - Data Shape (v1.0)]].

A ''marker'' is a tiddler, a ''vocabulary'' is a tag set, and a tiddler ''activates'' a vocabulary via its type field or a pragma.

[img[cm-v1-concept.svg]]

!! The three pieces

; ① A marker is a tiddler
: Tagged `$:/tags/CustomMarkup/Marker` plus the vocab tiddler's title (e.g. `[[vocab/fountain]]`). The `kind` field decides which matching mode applies; `open` is the literal that triggers it. Everything else is opt-in; see [[Overview - Data Shape (v1.0)]] § Marker fields.

; ② Vocabularies group markers
: One meta tiddler per vocab, tagged `$:/tags/CustomMarkup/Vocabulary`, named `vocab/<lowercase-caption>` by convention. A marker belongs to the vocab whose title is in its `tags` — there's no separate marker list on the vocabulary.

; ③ Two activation paths
:* ''Type field:'' `type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki;vocab=Default,Markdown`. Persisted, single `.tid` on disk.
:* ''Pragma:'' `\importcustom [tag[vocab/fountain]]` at the top of a tiddler. The filter runs over `[all[shadows+tiddlers]]`.
: A bare `text/vnd.tiddlywiki` (no `;vocab=`) implicitly activates `vocab/default`. Listing any `;vocab=` makes Default no longer implicit — add it explicitly if you want its markers.

!! The five marker kinds

; glyph
: Single fire at line start; whole line is body. Example: [[vocab/default/DOT]] (`. text` → `<div class="wltc wltc-dot">text</div>`).
; glyph-level
: N repetitions of `open` → emits class `wltc-lN` (default `max-level: 4`). Example: [[vocab/default/ANGLE]] (`»`, `»»`, ...).
; word
: Keyword block; single line (`mode: inline`) or multi-block. Example: [[vocab/fountain/INT]] (`INT. KITCHEN — MORNING`).
; inline-pair
: `open` ... `close` anywhere on a line. Example: [[vocab/default/SLASH]] (`/° ... °/`).
; list-item
: Consecutive items collapse into one container (`ul` / `ol` / `dl` / `blockquote`); nesting via indent. Example: [[vocab/markdown/ITEM-DASH]] (`- ...`).

!! Vocabulary collisions

When two activated vocabs ship a marker with the same `open` literal, the ''LAST'' listed in the type field wins. `;vocab=A,B` lets B's marker take over a shared `open`; `;vocab=B,A` lets A's win. This is how a vocab's own marker can intercept a literal that would otherwise belong to Default — see [[Vocabulary - Fountain]] for the canonical example.

